- Support implementation of the Common Alerting Protocol (CAP) and warning dissemination arrangements;

- Coordinate hazard, vulnerability and risk assessments, risk profiling and preparedness planning;

- Support development of hazard maps, evacuation plans and warning protocols'

- Promote impact-based forecasting, anticipatory action and community feedback mechanisms to improve warning effectiveness.

Coordinate community resilience training and stakeholder engagements

- Coordinate Community-Based Disaster Risk Management (CBDRM) training programmes and community resilience initiatives across the Division;

- Support communities to prepare, review and test Community Disaster Risk Management Plans;

- Promote inclusive participation of women, youth, and persons with disabilities, older persons and vulnerable groups in disaster risk management;

- Coordinate community awareness, risk communication and behavioral change programmes;

- Strengthen partnerships with Government agencies, Provincial Councils, Municipal Councils, NGOs, OPDs, faith-based organizations, traditional leaders, development partners and the private sector;

- Facilitate Divisional, Provincial, Municipal, District and Community Disaster Risk Management Committee meetings and stakeholder consultations.

Coordinate emergency operations and response

- Support the Divisional Commissioner in coordinating disaster preparedness, response, relief and recovery operations;

- Coordinate activation and management of the Divisional Emergency Operations Centre (DEOC);

- Coordinate operational information management, situation reporting and inter-agency response;

- Facilitate Initial Damage Assessments (IDA), Post-Disaster Needs Assessments (PDNA) and recovery planning;

